l_id": "toolu_01GKmb7cfdgsgQkGfxY96utP", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 57369, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01GKmb7cfdgsgQkGfxY96utP", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 59830, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_016Vcw9cmJ5Z2yMKRnYBJ94N", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 60130, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_016Vcw9cmJ5Z2yMKRnYBJ94N", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 60130, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_016Vcw9cmJ5Z2yMKRnYBJ94N", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 66091, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened a SEV2 incident, **INC-0001**, which pages the on-call engineer.\n\n**Rollback**\n- **Before:** v2.3.1 was live in us-east, us-west and eu-west. It was failing health checks with an 18% error rate.\n- **Version chosen:** v2.3.0 is the newest release marked healthy. The v2.3.1 release candidate before it was also unhealthy.\n- **First attempt:** it stopped after us-east because of an error in the deployment system. That left us-east on v2.3.0 and the other two regions on v2.3.1. I tried again once, since rolling back to a version that's known to be healthy is safe to repeat.\n- **Second attempt:** it worked. All regions are now on v2.3.0, the service reports healthy, and the error rate is 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- The request to create the incident timed out. I checked the incident list before trying again and found it had been created, so I didn't submit it a second time and page the on-call twice.\n- INC-0001 is open. It describes the failure, the rollback (including the first attempt that stopped partway) and the current state.\n- It lists two follow-ups: find out why v2.3.1 failed, and look into the deployment-system error.\n\nv2.3.1 shouldn't be redeployed until the cause is fixed.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_014tYDTZyejUxXscA7HTTvEJ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01J2Cc6FVExBGc2v6DZPYfPx", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_018KqLrV2YJ2ynD5jDtD1hd8", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_015pGP1s1bEZAHGYn2GDzPGz", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback stopped partway: us-east is on v2.3.0, but us-west and eu-west are still on v2.3.1. Rolling back to a known-healthy version is safe to repeat, so I'll try it once more.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01NffmWyK9TTzJb7YDQU7fog", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01EoC7tRN6eWwyRkyy1jdhxh", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01HNeSG1Nf2xEqsqCQR4uF9h", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01GKmb7cfdgsgQkGfxY96utP", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the deploy of v2.3.1 (unhealthy, error rate 18% in us-east, us-west and eu-west). I rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release. The first rollback attempt stopped partway with an orchestrator error after us-east, which left the regions on mixed versions (us-east v2.3.0, us-west/eu-west v2.3.1). A retry finished successfully. All regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) are now on v2.3.0. The service reports healthy with a 0.2% error rate. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure (v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy before release) and look into the orchestrator error during the rollback."}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The request timed out, so the incident may or may not have been created. I'll check before retrying so the on-call isn't paged twice.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_016Vcw9cmJ5Z2yMKRnYBJ94N", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened a SEV2 incident, **INC-0001**, which pages the on-call engineer.\n\n**Rollback**\n- **Before:** v2.3.1 was live in us-east, us-west and eu-west. It was failing health checks with an 18% error rate.\n- **Version chosen:** v2.3.0 is the newest release marked healthy. The v2.3.1 release candidate before it was also unhealthy.\n- **First attempt:** it stopped after us-east because of an error in the deployment system. That left us-east on v2.3.0 and the other two regions on v2.3.1. I tried again once, since rolling back to a version that's known to be healthy is safe to repeat.\n- **Second attempt:** it worked. All regions are now on v2.3.0, the service reports healthy, and the error rate is 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- The request to create the incident timed out. I checked the incident list before trying again and found it had been created, so I didn't submit it a second time and page the on-call twice.\n- INC-0001 is open. It describes the failure, the rollback (including the first attempt that stopped partway) and the current state.\n- It lists two follow-ups: find out why v2.3.1 failed, and look into the deployment-system error.\n\nv2.3.1 shouldn't be redeployed until the cause is fixed.", "type": "text"}]}]}